    {
      "slug": "sodium-extra",
      "stage": "optimizations",
      "published_version": {
        "author_id": "QXAY01zS",
        "changelog": "### Changed\r\n\r\n- Ported Sodium Extra to Minecraft 26.3.\r\n- Reworked Reduce Resolution on macOS to use SDL's high pixel-density window handling.\r\n- Improved planar and custom fog distance handling.\r\n\r\n### Removed\r\n\r\n- Removed the Wayland/XWayland Fullscreen Resolution option and recovery flow; Sodium now provides this support.\r\n- Removed the legacy macOS OpenGL and Vulkan framebuffer/presentation workarounds; SDL now handles the required window scaling.\r\n\r\n### Fixed\r\n\r\n- Fixed Panini Projection scaling with the active FOV.\r\n- Fixed blank tooltip translations.\r\n- Fixed custom fog distance encoding and preservation.\r\n- Improved fog rendering compatibility by avoiding a Redirect.\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/FlashyReese/sodium-extra/compare/mc26.2-0.9.4...mc26.3-0.9.4",
